3. Harmony (0Harmony.dll)
-------------------------
Project : Harmony, https://github.com/pardeike/Harmony
Licence : MIT

Harmony is what installs the runtime patches: the mod creates one `Harmony` instance per rollback group at
startup and calls `Patch` on it. The assembly ships with Slay the Spire 2 and is not redistributed here — the
mod references it at compile time and uses the copy the game has already loaded.


4. Godot Engine / GodotSharp
----------------------------
Project : Godot Engine, https://godotengine.org
Licence : MIT

`GodotSharp.dll` is part of the game installation and is not redistributed here. The patch uses it at
runtime to read and write Control properties and to build the few widgets it adds (a header row, a scroll-bar
hook), all inside the game's own Godot host.


